  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q62-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "62",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.\n$$\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{2(x-2)}{(x-5)(x+1)(x+5)}$, $x\\ne-5,-1,5$.\n\nFactorise both denominators, then combine over their common denominator.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}&=\\frac1{(x-5)(x+5)}+\\frac1{(x+1)(x+5)}\\\\\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}&=\\frac{(x+1)+(x-5)}{(x-5)(x+1)(x+5)}\\\\\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}&=\\frac{2(x-2)}{(x-5)(x+1)(x+5)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne-5,-1,5$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
